WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.600
"Oh no!" cried Ben. "Something happened to Waldo!"

2
00:00:05.601 --> 00:00:10.314
He tried to continue floating through the door of the science lab, but he was stuck.

3
00:00:10.315 --> 00:00:12.782
Ben cringed from embarrassment.

4
00:00:12.783 --> 00:00:18.776
Here he was—stuck halfway through a door—with everybody looking at him!

5
00:00:18.777 --> 00:00:22.748
"What happened to Waldo?" called Mr. Freaky.

6
00:00:22.749 --> 00:00:26.913
Ben tried to answer, but the science lab was soundproof.

7
00:00:26.914 --> 00:00:30.637
So no one could hear Ben yelling back to Mr. Freaky.

8
00:00:30.638 --> 00:00:38.205
Then suddenly— crash! The door was ripped off its hinges, and Gaby stormed into the

9
00:00:38.206 --> 00:00:43.346
lab. Ben landed hard on the

10
00:00:43.347 --> 00:00:49.715
floor. "Waldo!" Gaby cried. "What happened to you? Waldo, please wake

11
00:00:49.716 --> 00:00:54.004
up!" Mr. Freaky and the human adults rushed into the

12
00:00:54.005 --> 00:00:58.408
room. "Someone get the school nurse!" Mr. Freaky

13
00:00:58.409 --> 00:01:05.034
shouted. Mog and some other students stood in the

14
00:01:05.035 --> 00:01:09.125
doorway. Minutes later the nurse slipped through the

15
00:01:09.126 --> 00:01:12.888
crowd. "Excuse me, dear," she said to

16
00:01:12.889 --> 00:01:20.871
Gaby. Gaby backed away as Mrs. Germ checked Waldo's

17
00:01:20.872 --> 00:01:26.859
pulse. The nurse opened one of Waldo's eyes and shined a light in

18
00:01:26.860 --> 00:01:31.102
it. "He'll be fine," she

19
00:01:31.103 --> 00:01:34.197
declared. Ben was relieved that Waldo was

20
00:01:34.198 --> 00:01:42.060
okay. He was also relieved that nobody was talking about how he'd gotten stuck in the

21
00:01:42.061 --> 00:01:50.909
door. Waldo opened his eyes and moaned. "Oh . . . What's going on? Where am

22
00:01:50.910 --> 00:01:54.538
I?" "You're in the science lab," said Mr.

23
00:01:54.539 --> 00:01:57.458
Freaky. "Can you tell us what happened to

24
00:01:57.459 --> 00:02:03.693
you?" Waldo sat up and rubbed his

25
00:02:03.694 --> 00:02:08.592
head. "The last thing I remember, I was standing in here, waiting for

26
00:02:08.593 --> 00:02:12.411
Deb." "Deb?" cried Mog and Gaby at the same

27
00:02:12.412 --> 00:02:18.778
time. "Um, yeah," said Waldo. "She offered to help me with the

28
00:02:18.779 --> 00:02:22.106
experiment." He glanced at the mess on the floor and

29
00:02:22.107 --> 00:02:26.703
sighed. "I guess my experiment is

30
00:02:26.704 --> 00:02:31.391
ruined." "Oh, Waldo," Gaby gushed. "You don't need her

31
00:02:31.392 --> 00:02:34.232
help! You're so much smarter than she

32
00:02:34.233 --> 00:02:41.845
is." Mog looked insulted. "What are you talking about? Deb is super

33
00:02:41.846 --> 00:02:46.797
smart!" He paused. "But I agree that she doesn't need to help

34
00:02:46.798 --> 00:02:50.158
Waldo. She should just hang out with me

35
00:02:50.159 --> 00:02:55.154
today." Mog scratched his head. "Where is Deb

36
00:02:55.155 --> 00:03:01.035
anyway?" "And where is Winnie?" a witch asked. "I haven't seen her all

37
00:03:01.036 --> 00:03:07.518
day." "Winnie is working on a . . . special assignment for me," said Miss

38
00:03:07.519 --> 00:03:12.731
Bungle. Ben perked up. Winnie was working on a special

39
00:03:12.732 --> 00:03:16.232
assignment? "Deb never showed up," said

40
00:03:16.233 --> 00:03:21.870
Waldo. Mr. Freaky wrung his hands. "We need to find out where Deb

41
00:03:21.871 --> 00:03:26.187
is. Miss Bungle, can you please ask the office ogre to look for Deb?"

42
00:03:26.188 --> 00:03:32.625
"Of course," said the broom flying teacher, who then hurried out of the room.

43
00:03:32.626 --> 00:03:39.493
Mr. Freaky glanced around the lab. "Waldo, do you remember anything else?"

44
00:03:39.494 --> 00:03:44.837
Waldo nodded. "Yes, a human girl ran into the lab."

45
00:03:44.838 --> 00:03:49.086
Mayor Hubbletree looked startled. "What?"

46
00:03:49.087 --> 00:03:53.686
"It must be the same girl who ran into the school," Ben put in.

47
00:03:53.687 --> 00:03:55.701
"I saw her too."

48
00:03:55.702 --> 00:03:58.828
"You did?" said Mr. Freaky.

49
00:03:58.829 --> 00:04:03.132
Ben nodded. "About Winnie, though, do you know where—?"

50
00:04:03.133 --> 00:04:06.402
"I don't believe it!" Mayor Hubbletree interrupted.

51
00:04:06.403 --> 00:04:11.112
"You heard Ms. Prim, Freaky. None of our students is missing."

52
00:04:11.113 --> 00:04:15.050
"A human was in here," Waldo insisted.

53
00:04:15.051 --> 00:04:18.567
"She seemed really scared and confused."

54
00:04:18.568 --> 00:04:21.058
The mayor folded his arms.

55
00:04:21.059 --> 00:04:25.288
"Can you blame her? This place gives me the creeps."

56
00:04:25.289 --> 00:04:31.871
Waldo continued. "I asked her who she was and what she was doing here, but she wouldn't tell me.

57
00:04:31.872 --> 00:04:36.341
She said something like, 'I don't understand what's going on.'

58
00:04:36.342 --> 00:04:39.891
Then she saw her reflection and shrieked.

59
00:04:39.892 --> 00:04:43.133
I don't remember anything after that."

60
00:04:43.134 --> 00:04:46.094
Gaby's face grew red with anger.

61
00:04:46.095 --> 00:04:49.608
"Whoever that girl is, she must have knocked you out!

62
00:04:49.609 --> 00:04:53.256
If I ever get my hands on her, I'll—"

63
00:04:53.257 --> 00:04:57.003
"This is outrageous!" boomed Mayor Hubbletree.

64
00:04:57.004 --> 00:05:02.365
"The idea that a human would come in here and attack a monster is absurd!"

65
00:05:02.366 --> 00:05:07.803
"Do you think that crazy human hurt Deb too?" Mog asked Waldo.

66
00:05:07.804 --> 00:05:11.282
"Of course not!" shouted Mayor Hubbletree.

67
00:05:11.283 --> 00:05:14.544
"Everyone knows that it's monsters who attack humans!

68
00:05:14.545 --> 00:05:16.975
Not the other way around!"

69
00:05:16.976 --> 00:05:24.897
Mr. Freaky pulled out a handkerchief and blew his noses.

70
00:05:24.898 --> 00:05:32.030
"Maybe it was a human, but she didn't mean to hurt Waldo," said Dave.

71
00:05:32.031 --> 00:05:36.958
"After all, I caused the purple spot epidemic by accident.

72
00:05:36.959 --> 00:05:40.337
Or maybe something went wrong with the experiment."

73
00:05:40.338 --> 00:05:46.202
The mayor nodded. "Yes, it was probably something to do with the experiment."

74
00:05:46.203 --> 00:05:52.950
Now Waldo looked annoyed. "My experiment was going fine."

75
00:05:52.951 --> 00:05:57.768
"Was the human wearing a hoodie with a green skull on the back?" Ben blurted out.

76
00:05:57.769 --> 00:06:02.406
Waldo looked surprised. "Actually, yes, she was."

77
00:06:02.407 --> 00:06:08.640
Just then Ms. Prim came back into the lab with her clipboard.

78
00:06:08.641 --> 00:06:10.936
"I've done another head count, Mayor.

79
00:06:10.937 --> 00:06:15.447
All of our students are here. No one is missing."

80
00:06:15.448 --> 00:06:21.343
"There you go, Freaky," said Mayor Hubbletree, looking around at the monsters.

81
00:06:21.344 --> 00:06:26.801
"It wasn't a human who caused this mess. That means—"

82
00:06:26.802 --> 00:06:31.906
"It was a monster!" Mr. Freaky put his head in his hands.

83
00:06:31.907 --> 00:06:38.363
"Everything is totally out of control!"

